; TITHE - title theme, option 2: THE RECKONING
;
; A jig in E dorian - the reference game's own colour, E minor with a raised
; sixth and D major as its other pole. A row is an EIGHTH of THREE ticks, so a
; bar of 6/8 is six rows and the dotted-quarter beat is 121 BPM. The fiddle
; tunes up over a bodhran, then plays an AABB tune: A low and turning, B up
; an octave and landing back on E. Lute chords on the off-beats, a plucked
; bass on the beats - the "boom-chick" every session band plays.

song reckoning "The Reckoning"
groove 3
unit 8
rows 12
measure 6
voice lead fiddle
voice bass pluckbass
voice chord lute

; --- the fiddle tunes up ------------------------------------------------------
lead LI = o4 l8 e <b> e g e <b> | > e <b> e d e f+ |
bass BI = o2 l4. e e | e e |
chord CI = o3 r1. |
drum DI = t8 p8 p8 t8 p8 p8 | t8 p8 p8 t8 t8 t8 |

; --- A: twice, the second time handing on to B -----------------------------------
lead LA1 = o4 l8 b4 a g f+ e | f+4 d d e f+ |
lead LA2 = o4 l8 g4 a b4 >e | d c+< b a f+ d |
lead LA3 = o4 l8 b4 a g f+ e | f+4 a >d4 c+< |
lead LA4 = o4 l8 b a g a4 f+ | e4. e4 d |
lead LA5 = o4 l8 b a g a4 f+ | e4. e4 >d |
; --- B: up an octave ------------------------------------------------------------
lead LB1 = o5 l8 e4 f+ g4 e | d4 e f+4 d |
lead LB2 = o5 l8 e f+ g f+ e d | <b4 a f+4 a> |
lead LB3 = o5 l8 e4 f+ g4 a | b4 a g4 f+ |
lead LB4 = o5 l8 e d <b a f+ a | b4. >d4. |
lead LB5 = o5 l8 e d <b a f+ a | b4. e4.> |

; the bass on the beats, the chord on the off-beats
bass BEm = o2 l4. e b | d a |
bass BEd = o2 l4. e b | d f+ |
bass BEe = o2 l4. e b | e e |
bass BBD = o2 l4. e b | d a |
bass BBe = o2 l4. e d | e e |
chord CEm = o3 r4 [e g b]8 r4 [e g b]8 | r4 [d f+ a]8 r4 [d f+ a]8 |
chord CEe = o3 r4 [e g b]8 r4 [e g b]8 | r4 [e g b]8 r4 [e b]8 |
chord CDm = o3 r4 [e g b]8 r4 [e g b]8 | r4 [d f+ a]8 r4 [c+ f+ a]8 |
chord CBe = o3 r4 [e g b]8 r4 [d f+ a]8 | r4 [e g b]8 r4 [e g b]8 |

drum DJ = t8 p8 p8 t8 p8 p8 | t8 p8 p8 t8 p8 p8 |
drum DF = t8 p8 p8 t8 p8 p8 | t8 p8 t8 T8 T8 T8 |

; AABB, as a session plays it: each part twice, the second time with the
; ending that hands on
order LI BI CI DI
order LA1 BEm CEm DJ          ; 1: the loop comes back here
order LA2 BEd CDm DJ
order LA3 BEm CEm DJ
order LA4 BEe CEe DF
order LA1 BEm CEm DJ
order LA2 BEd CDm DJ
order LA3 BEm CEm DJ
order LA5 BEe CEe DF
order LB1 BBD CEm DJ
order LB2 BEd CDm DJ
order LB3 BBD CEm DJ
order LB4 BBe CBe DF
order LB1 BBD CEm DJ
order LB2 BEd CDm DJ
order LB3 BBD CEm DJ
order LB5 BBe CBe DF
loop 1
